 "youtube": {
  "title": "Brooklyn Bridge: The Woman Who Saved It Without a Degree",
  "description": "The Brooklyn Bridge was finished by a woman with no engineering degree. So how did Emily Roebling end up at the heart of one of the greatest building projects of the 1800s?\n\nIts designer John Roebling died in 1869, before construction began. His son Washington took over and worked in the pressurized caissons under the East River until caisson disease, the bends, left him an invalid. Watching from his window with a telescope, he relied on his wife Emily, who studied the engineering, carried his orders and dealt with the engineers. Just before the bridge opened in May 1883, Emily was the first to ride across it.\n\nSubscribe to Stickstory for a new true story every day. Who is the forgotten hero you think deserves more credit? Tell me in the comments!\n\n#shorts #brooklynbridge #emilyroebling #history #stickstory",
